why Redemption at 12, the paladin's resurrection: an easy chain through your capital and its home zone.

# The level 12 Redemption chain of the Alliance paladins, one guide for both
# races with `only` steps:
# - Human: Tome of Divinity (2998 from Brother Wilhelm in Goldshire, or 3681
#   from Brandur Ironhammer in Ironforge; they close each other) to Duthorian
#   Rall, The Tome of Divinity (1641, Duthorian hands you the book; repeatable,
#   so he gives a new one if it is lost), 1642 (read the book), 1643
#   (Stephanie Turner), 1644 (10 Linen Cloth), 1780, 1781 (Gazin Tenorm, the
#   Symbol of Life), 1786 (revive Henze Faulk in Elwynn), 1787 (the Defias
#   Script) and 1788 (Redemption from Duthorian).
# - Dwarf: Tome of Divinity (2997 Azar Stronghammer in Kharanos, 2999 Brandur
#   Ironhammer in Ironforge or 3000 Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in Stormwind;
#   one closes the others) to Tiza Battleforge, The Tome of Divinity (1645,
#   repeatable, the book), 1646, 1647 (John Turner), 1648 (10 Linen Cloth),
#   1778, 1779 (Muiredon Battleforge, the Symbol of Life), 1783 (revive Narm
#   Faulk in Dun Morogh), 1784 (the Dark Iron Script) and 1785 (Redemption from
#   Tiza).
# The Symbol of Life (1790 Human, 1789 Dwarf) is the replacement quest for a
# lost symbol: named in the tips only.
# Sources: Forever's quest data (quests.json, the knowledge base) for givers,
# enders, objectives, the exclusive breadcrumbs and the drop rates (Defias
# Script 50% from the Defias Rogue Wizards, Dark Iron Script 50% from the Dark
# Iron Spies); the Forever server tables (TDB) for the chain order, the books
# (1641 rewards item 6775, 1645 item 6916, both repeatable) and Redemption
# (1788 and 1785 teach spell 7329); players' notes in Forever's quest data
# for where the bodies lie (Henze on a mound of the Heroes' Vigil island in
# Stone Cairn Lake, Narm on the smallest of three hills between Helm's Bed Lake
# and the Dark Iron camp) and the Defias mages on the island. Warcraft Wiki
# (Stephanie Turner) for her place: the middle of the Trade District, outside
# a general goods store.
# The leveling routes do this chain in pieces (Human: forever/alliance/
# 02-westfall, 04-redridge-mountains, 05-duskwood; Dwarf: forever/alliance/
# dwarf-gnome/01-dun-morogh); this guide is the whole chain in one go.
# Forsaken paladins learn Redemption from A Lesson in Divinity
# (forever/class/paladin/tyrs-watch).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The summons

step The summons (Human)
  only Human
  tip At 12 Brother Wilhelm, the paladin trainer in Goldshire, sends you to Duthorian Rall in Stormwind's Cathedral of Light. The errand is optional, a little XP: Brandur Ironhammer in Ironforge gives the same one (taking one closes the other), and Duthorian starts the chain without it.
  level 12
  accept 2998 optional                -- Brother Wilhelm, Goldshire

step The summons (Dwarf)
  only Dwarf
  tip At 12 Brandur Ironhammer, the paladin trainer in Ironforge's Mystic Ward, sends you upstairs to Tiza Battleforge. The errand is optional, a little XP: Azar Stronghammer in Kharanos and Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in Stormwind give the same one (taking one closes the others), and Tiza starts the chain without it.
  level 12
  accept 2999 optional                -- Brandur Ironhammer, Ironforge

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Human: Stormwind

step Duthorian Rall
  only Human
  zone Stormwind City
  when onquest 2998
  turnin 2998                         -- Duthorian Rall, Cathedral of Light

step Duthorian Rall
  only Human
  zone Stormwind City
  when onquest 3681
  turnin 3681                         -- Duthorian Rall, Cathedral of Light

step The Tome of Divinity
  only Human
  zone Stormwind City
  tip Duthorian Rall stands inside the Cathedral of Light. He hands you the Tome of Divinity: right-click it in your bags to start the next quest. If the book says the quest is already done, destroy it and ask Duthorian for a new copy. Bring 10 Linen Cloth for the next step if you have it.
  turnin 1641 direct                  -- Duthorian Rall
  accept 1642 item 6775               -- Right-click the Tome of Divinity
  turnin 1642                         -- Duthorian Rall
  accept 1643

step Stephanie Turner
  only Human
  zone Stormwind City
  tip Stephanie Turner stands at a corner in the middle of the Trade District, outside a general goods store. She wants 10 Linen Cloth: humanoids drop it (Riverpaw gnolls in Westfall about every other kill, Defias and kobolds a little less), or buy it at the Auction House a few steps away in the Trade District.
  turnin 1643                         -- Stephanie Turner
  accept 1644
  collect 2589 quest 1644.1 @61.2,71.3 live -- Linen Cloth x10: humanoids, or the Auction House
  turnin 1644
  accept 1780

step The Symbol of Life
  only Human
  zone Stormwind City
  tip Back to the Cathedral. Duthorian gives you the Symbol of Life; Gazin Tenorm lies wounded by the altar of the same hall. Keep the symbol: you need it on Henze Faulk. If you lose it, Duthorian gives you another (The Symbol of Life).
  turnin 1780                         -- Duthorian Rall
  accept 1781
  turnin 1781                         -- Gazin Tenorm
  accept 1786

step Henze Faulk
  only Human
  zone Elwynn Forest
  tip Henze Faulk lies dead on Heroes' Vigil, the island in Stone Cairn Lake in eastern Elwynn, on top of one of the mounds around the stone circle. Target his body and use the Symbol of Life to raise him, then speak to him. If another paladin just raised him, his body is back within about three minutes. The Defias Rogue Wizards on the island (level 9-10) cast Frostbolt from far off: they stand apart, so pull one at a time.
  use 6866 quest 1786.1 @72.6,51.41   -- Symbol of Life on Henze Faulk's body
  turnin 1786                         -- Henze Faulk
  accept 1787

step The Defias Script
  only Human
  zone Elwynn Forest
  tip The Defias Rogue Wizards around the big stone tablet east of Henze carry the Defias Script: about one kill in two drops it, but some players need many kills. They respawn in three minutes.
  collect 6846 quest 1787.1 @74.16,52.0 -- Defias Script: Defias Rogue Wizards

step Redemption
  only Human
  zone Stormwind City
  tip Back to the Cathedral of Light: Gazin takes the script, Duthorian teaches you Redemption.
  turnin 1787                         -- Gazin Tenorm
  accept 1788
  turnin 1788                         -- Duthorian Rall: Redemption

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Dwarf: Ironforge

step Tiza Battleforge
  only Dwarf
  zone Ironforge
  when onquest 2997
  turnin 2997                         -- Tiza Battleforge, upstairs in the Hall of Mysteries

step Tiza Battleforge
  only Dwarf
  zone Ironforge
  when onquest 2999
  turnin 2999                         -- Tiza Battleforge, upstairs in the Hall of Mysteries

step Tiza Battleforge
  only Dwarf
  zone Ironforge
  when onquest 3000
  turnin 3000                         -- Tiza Battleforge, upstairs in the Hall of Mysteries

step The Tome of Divinity
  only Dwarf
  zone Ironforge
  tip Tiza Battleforge stands upstairs in the Hall of Mysteries, in the Mystic Ward: take the ramp at the back of the hall. She hands you the Tome of Divinity: right-click it in your bags to start the next quest. If the book says the quest is already done, destroy it and ask Tiza for a new copy. Bring 10 Linen Cloth for the next step if you have it.
  turnin 1645 direct                  -- Tiza Battleforge
  accept 1646 item 6916               -- Right-click the Tome of Divinity
  turnin 1646                         -- Tiza Battleforge
  accept 1647

step John Turner
  only Dwarf
  zone Ironforge
  tip John Turner walks the outer ring of the Commons, past the front gate, the bank and the Auction House. He wants 10 Linen Cloth: humanoids drop it (Kogan Forgestone in Kharanos every time, Dark Iron Ambushers about two kills in five), or buy it at the Auction House on his ring.
  turnin 1647                         -- John Turner
  accept 1648
  collect 2589 quest 1648.1 @24.2,74.7 -- Linen Cloth x10: humanoids, or the Auction House
  turnin 1648
  accept 1778

step The Symbol of Life
  only Dwarf
  zone Ironforge
  tip Back upstairs in the Hall of Mysteries. Tiza gives you the Symbol of Life; her husband Muiredon Battleforge rests on the same floor. Keep the symbol: you need it on Narm Faulk. If you lose it, Tiza gives you another (The Symbol of Life).
  turnin 1778                         -- Tiza Battleforge
  accept 1779
  turnin 1779                         -- Muiredon Battleforge
  accept 1783

step Narm Faulk
  only Dwarf
  zone Dun Morogh
  tip Narm Faulk lies dead in Dun Morogh, not Loch Modan: east past Kharanos, north-east of Ironband's compound, on the smallest of three little hills between Helm's Bed Lake and the Dark Iron camp. Target his body and use the Symbol of Life to raise him, then speak to him. If another paladin just raised him, his body is back within about three minutes.
  use 6866 quest 1783.1 @78.32,58.09  -- Symbol of Life on Narm Faulk's body
  turnin 1783                         -- Narm Faulk
  accept 1784

step The Dark Iron Script
  only Dwarf
  zone Dun Morogh
  tip The Dark Iron Spies (level 9-11, twelve of them) sneak around the little house below the lake, just south of Narm; you see them from his hill. About one kill in two drops the Dark Iron Script. They run for help at low health: finish them or step back. They respawn in three minutes.
  collect 6847 quest 1784.1 @77.53,61.18 -- Dark Iron Script: Dark Iron Spies

step Redemption
  only Dwarf
  zone Ironforge
  tip Back up to the Hall of Mysteries: Muiredon takes the script, Tiza teaches you Redemption.
  turnin 1784                         -- Muiredon Battleforge
  accept 1785
  turnin 1785                         -- Tiza Battleforge: Redemption
